es y la biología, proporcionando la base para el desarrollo de nuevas terapias.", "INVESTIGACIÓN EPIDEMIOLÓGICA:La investigación epidemiológica se centra en el estudio de la distribución y determinantes de la salud y enfermedades en poblaciones, ayudando a establecer relaciones causales.", "NUTRIGENÓMICA:La nutrigenómica es un campo de estudio que investiga cómo los nutrientes afectan la expresión genética y cómo la genética influye en la respuesta a los nutrientes.", "REAL DECRETO 1090/2015:Real Decreto 1090/2015 is the legislation that regulates clinical trials with medications in Spain, focusing on ethical and methodological standards for trials.", "AGENCIA ESPAÑOLA DE MEDICAMENTOS Y PRODUCTOS SANITARIOS:The Agencia Española de Medicamentos y Productos Sanitarios is the Spanish Agency responsible for the regulation and oversight of medications and clinical trials.", "LEY ORGÁNICA 15/1999:Ley Orgánica 15/1999 is the Spanish law concerning the protection of personal data, ensuring the privacy of individuals involved in clinical trials.", "DECLARACIÓN DE HELSINKI:The Declaration of Helsinki outlines ethical principles for medical research involving human subjects, which must be adhered to in clinical trials.", "ESTUDIOS POSTAUTORIZACIÓN:Post-authorization studies are observational studies conducted with approved medications to monitor their effects in the general population.", "REAL DECRETO 577/2013:", "COMITÉS DE ÉTICA DE LA INVESTIGACIÓN:Comités de Ética de la Investigación are ethical committees that oversee clinical trials to ensure they meet ethical standards.", "REGISTRO ESPAÑOL DE ESTUDIOS CLÍNICOS:Registro Español de Estudios Clínicos is the official registry for clinical studies conducted in Spain, ensuring transparency and compliance with regulations.", "AGENCIA ESPAÑOLA DEL MEDICAMENTO:The Agencia Española del Medicamento is the Spanish agency tasked with the regulation and oversight of medications and clinical trials. As a regulatory body in Spain, it is responsible for the evaluation and supervision of both medicines and medical devices, ensuring their safety, efficacy, and quality for public health.", "CIBER:CIBER, which stands for Centros de Investigación Biomédica en Red, is a consortium in Spain designed to enhance biomedical research and health sciences. It serves as a cooperative research structure that aims to promote and strengthen research and development in health by incorporating new thematic areas and research groups. Through its collaborative approach, CIBER seeks to advance the field of biomedical research and improve health outcomes."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}